  "note": "Two-column verso body page, 1750x2180 px (ratio 0.803, not A4). body_text_size_px=20 (cap-to-baseline; prose line pitch 35 px, the two display lists use a looser 43 px pitch but the same type size). ONE UNCERTAINTY, the same kind as p025 and p026: block 8 is a single paragraph that runs across the column break -- its first two lines sit at the foot of the LEFT column and its next nine lines open the RIGHT column. I put n=8 on the left-column region and n=null on the right-column continuation region rather than repeat the same n twice; that null paragraph is the tail of block 8, not an unmatched block. Table 2.4 (n=11) has TWO fills: a lavender header row #e0deef (y 0.4055-0.4330) over peach body rows #ffe4b8. I report the body fill on the table element, which covers the whole bordered table, and emit the header row immediately after as a nested unnumbered tinted box carrying #e0deef, so neither colour is lost; those two regions therefore overlap by design. The cyan table caption 'Table 2.4 Subshell Notations' sits outside the table border and is emitted separately as an unnumbered table_caption (#00adef bold sans; the allowed font list has no sans-italic/bold variants so I report 'sans'). No page_header_band, rule_bar or footer_rule on this page: furniture is the running head (STRUCTURE OF ATOM left, page number 55 right) and the centred '2024-25' footer line, labelled running_header because it is a running footer rather than the page number. A diagonal '(C) NCERT not to be republished' watermark crosses both columns; not emitted as an element."
